extends layout

block content
  .page.page--narrow
    article.article
      span.kicker Write for us
      h1 Share a place you love
      p.article__summary
        | Streets is written by locals. If there's a café, gallery, mural, shop or corner of your
        | city that more people should know about, we'd love to hear about it.
      p
        a.btn(href=base + 'submit.html') Send us a story

      .article__body
        h2 What we publish
        p
          strong Places.
          |  Short pieces of 150 to 300 words about one spot: why it's special, what to order or look
          | for, and who's behind it.
        p
          strong Stories.
          |  Longer pieces about the people, history and culture of a place. Local journalism, in
          | other words.
        p
          strong Walks.
          |  A route through three or more places, with a line or two on getting from one to the next.

        h2 What makes a good Streets place
        ul
          li Independent. No chains, and nothing that's already in every guide.
          li Somewhere you've actually been, recently, and would take a friend.
          li Somewhere with a story: a person, a history, a reason it exists.

        h2 How to write it
        ul
          li Write like you're telling a friend. Be specific: the dish, the painting, the view from the back table.
          li Say why it matters, not just what it is. No star ratings.
          li Include the address, and anything a first-timer needs to know.
          li Keep facts you can't check out of it. Opening times change, so don't list them.

        h2 Photos
        p
          | Photos make a place come alive. Send your own, or ones you have permission to use, and
          | tell us who took them so we can credit them. A link to a shared folder is fine.

        h2 Be fair
        ul
          li If you work at, own, or are friends with the people behind a place, tell us. It doesn't rule you out, but readers deserve to know.
          li We don't publish paid posts or anything written in exchange for free stuff.
          li Be kind. We don't publish takedowns of small businesses.

        h2 What happens next
        p
          | An editor reads every submission. We might ask you questions, and we'll edit for length and
          | clarity. We'll check the details before anything goes live. When your piece is published it
          | carries your name, with a writer page listing everything you've written.

        h2#new-city Starting Streets in a new city
        p
          | We add a city once it has a local editor and around twenty stories ready to go, so it never
          | launches empty. If you'd like to start one,
          |
          a(href=base + 'submit.html?type=city') tell us about your city
          | .
